-- title:
--   Completed local ring at a supersingular point descends to an unramified base
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $q$ lies in the maximal ideal and $\ell$ and $M'$ are invertible. Assume two variable-change stability hypotheses: every level-$\ell$ datum $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ over an $A$-algebra $T$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.IsLevelPStructure`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L104) for $W$ (both points on $W$, both $x$-coordinates roots of $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$, both independence elements units) continues to satisfy it for $C\bullet W$ after the transformation $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; and every $h$ with `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (a two-torsion kernel generator if $p^k=2$, otherwise a cyclic $p^k$-kernel generator of degree $\le\varphi(p^k)/2$ with leading coefficient $1$, dividing $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$ after multiplication by $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}}$ and dividing the relevant scaled numerators) transports to `kernelVariableChangeDeg`. Assume further group laws $\mathcal G$ on the projective models of discriminant-invertible Weierstrass curves over $A$-algebras that are chord–tangent (field-valued points identify with affine points, additively and Galois-equivariantly) and have the origin as identity, a level transport $\mathcal T$ of raw Drinfeld pairs for $\mathcal G$ and $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`, and the existence, for every curve, of graded ring homomorphisms realising variable changes and coefficient maps with the irrelevant-ideal condition (`IsVariableChangeHom`, `IsCoefficientHom`). Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the rigid data `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q` (the product of the $\Gamma_0$-prime-power component, the level-$\ell$ component and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component) with $P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A$, let $\mathfrak p$ be a minimal prime of $(0)$ in $P_0.B_0$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$ with $\varpi^{q-1}=\varepsilon q$ for a unit $\varepsilon$, let $\zeta\in A$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, let $xr$ be a raw point over $P_0.B_0$ whose class is the universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$, let $x$ be a maximal ideal of $P_0.B_0/\mathfrak p$ containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $F_0$ be a formal group over $(P_0.B_0/\mathfrak p)/x$ whose power series is the normalised formal group law of $xr.\mathrm{curve}$ reduced modulo $\mathfrak p$ and then $x$, such that $F_0.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q$ (the $q$-fold iterate of the group law in the first variable) equals a unit times $X^{q\cdot q}$. Then there exist a discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with maximal ideal generated by $q$ and finite residue field, together with the same package of hypotheses over $A_0$ (the two variable-change stability statements, group laws $\mathcal G_0$ chord–tangent with origin identity, a section transport $\mathcal T_0$, and the two graded-homomorphism hypotheses), a fine moduli package $P^u$ for `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q` with $P^u.B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, a raw point $xu$ whose class is $P^u.\mathrm{univ}$, a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m^u$ of $P^u.B_0$ containing the image of $q$, and a formal group $F_0^u$ over $P^u.B_0/\mathfrak m^u$ equal to the normalised formal group law of $xu.\mathrm{curve}$ modulo $\mathfrak m^u$ with $F_0^u.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q$ again a unit times $X^{q\cdot q}$, for which there is a ring isomorphism between the $x$-adic completion of $P_0.B_0/\mathfrak p$ and the $\mathfrak m^u$-adic completion of $P^u.B_0$.
--
--   This is the descent step passing from the completed local ring of an irreducible component of a full-level moduli ring over a base containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity (ramified of degree $q-1$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$) to the completed local ring of the corresponding package over an absolutely unramified discrete valuation ring, at a point where the universal formal group has height two. It is used in the proof that the residue field tensored with such an adic completion is reduced.
